    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0200" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg96"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mizner to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-09-09"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 9, 1890</date>.
                        (Received September 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 158.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your instructions by telegram of the 3d instant, which was received by me per
                    steamer from La Libertad on the 6th instant.</p>
                <pb facs="0201" n="97" xml:id="pg97"/>
                <p>Anticipating these instructions, I had the honor to make a report to you as full
                    as possible in my dispatch No. 150 of August 29, 1890, concurrently with that of
                    Consul-General Hosmer’s No. 243 of the same date. If any additional facts,
                    however, come to my knowledge in relation to the same matter, I shall promptly
                    make you acquainted with them, and shall obtain an affidavit of facts from
                    Captain Pitts, commander of the Pacific Mail steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Acapulco</hi>, when that vessel returns to the port of San José.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing B.
                    Mizner.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
